# Cubic zirconia (yttria-stabilised cubic ZrO2), the commonest diamond simulant. Measured by
# variable-angle spectroscopic ellipsometry on bulk crystal: Synowicki & Tiwald, Thin Solid Films
# 455-456, 248 (2004), doi:10.1016/j.tsf.2004.02.028; data CC0 via refractiveindex.info
# (ZrO2/nk/Synowicki, an oscillator model fitted to the measurement), resampled here to 5 nm.
# n_d 2.148, V_d 33.5; its fire (n at 430.8 nm minus n at 686.7 nm) is 0.060 against
# diamond's 0.044, which is why a CZ throws more coloured light than a diamond does.
# aliases: cz zirconia cubic-zirconia
